WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.690
RAWM starts from the orthogonal projector P of OWM,

00:00:03.770 --> 00:00:07.460
which points the update away from the subspace
spanned by previous inputs.

00:00:07.540 --> 00:00:11.230
On top of it,

00:00:11.310 --> 00:00:15.000
the method builds a second projector Q that is
orthogonal to P and scaled by the ratio

00:00:15.080 --> 00:00:18.770
beta of genuine to fake utterances in the batch.

00:00:18.850 --> 00:00:22.540
The two projectors are normalized and combined into
a modified direction R,

00:00:22.620 --> 00:00:26.310
so when a batch is mostly genuine the update leans
toward preserving old knowledge,

00:00:26.390 --> 00:00:30.080
and otherwise it leans toward learning the new data.

00:00:30.160 --> 00:00:33.850
For datasets recorded under very different conditions,

00:00:33.930 --> 00:00:37.620
a regularization term treats the frozen pre-trained
model as a teacher and forces the

00:00:37.700 --> 00:00:41.390
fine-tuned student to match its softened outputs,

00:00:41.470 --> 00:00:45.160
remembering the old inference distribution.

00:00:45.240 --> 00:00:48.930
Crucially, none of this replays past samples.
